 "why_floorplan": "SRAM tile of the X cluster (475.2 x 432 under xn): 8 SRAM in 2 columns x 4 rows (90.72 pitch: 20-um channels, the v1 SRAM LEF only sits on the snapped macro lattice so it cannot abut; y 43.2 .. 385.8: 43-um S halo over the kq pin band, 46-um N halo under the lw_* face); h0 column R0 at x 43.2 (read pins on the 43-um W channel), h1 column MY at x 257.04 (read pins on the E channel): each key half reads only its own column, so its mux runs down its own channel to the kq pin flops; write pins of both columns face the 39-um centre gap.  The ONLY pin-flop band is kq on the S face, clock entry at its SW corner (the rb geometry that passed R at 52 / 79 ps).",
